    "body": "## Why?\n\n- HiCache host pools fail to start when the process's cgroup membership sits above the cgroup mount root.\n- A common case: a Slurm `srun --overlap` step that joins another step's container. `/proc/self/cgroup` shows `0::/../../../step_147/user/task_0`.\n- `_cgroup_memory_headroom` raises `ValueError` in that case. `available_host_memory_bytes` only catches `OSError` and `RuntimeError`.\n- So even an explicit `--hicache-size` crashes at host-pool allocation. It should instead take the documented fallback, which checks explicitly sized pools against host available memory.\n\n## What?\n\n- `_cgroup_memory_headroom` raises `RuntimeError` for an unresolvable membership path. This matches the neighbouring \"cannot locate the process memory cgroup\" case.\n- Explicit sizing now falls back to host available memory, with the existing warning.\n- Auto-sizing keeps its strict behavior and still asks for `--hicache-size`.\n\n## Verification?\n\nProduction code only, inside a real `srun --overlap --container-name=...` step on an H200 node (observed):\n\n```text\n/proc/self/cgroup: 0::/../../../step_147/user/task_0\n\nhost_memory_budget_bytes(auto_size=...)\n                      Before (main)                     After (this PR)\nauto_size=False  ->   ValueError: Cannot resolve        1903.9 GiB (host fallback,\n                      cgroup memory path                warning logged)\nauto_size=True   ->   ValueError: Cannot resolve        RuntimeError: ... set\n                      cgroup memory path                --hicache-size explicitly\n```\n\nRepro: inside such a step, call `sglang.srt.mem_cache.pool_host.base.host_memory_budget_bytes(auto_size=False)`. Or launch any server with `--enable-hierarchical-cache --hicache-size <N>`.\n\n## Test?\n\n- New `test_membership_outside_mount_root_requires_explicit_sizing` in `test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_host_memory.py`, for cgroup v1 and v2.\n  - **observed:** fails on main (2 subtests, `ValueError`), passes with the fix.\n- `python test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_host_memory.py` (Linux, H200 node):\n  - **observed:** main 9 tests OK; this PR 10 tests OK.\n- `pre-commit run --files` on both changed files: **observed** passed.\n- CI: **pending**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39882324756](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39882324756)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39882324769](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39882324769)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39882324841](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39882324841)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
